# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# TypeScript source always diffs as TEXT, whatever bytes it happens to contain.
# `apps/web/src/viewer/propsView.ts` carried two NUL bytes as a search separator, and git
# therefore rendered every change to it as `Bin N -> M bytes`: no reviewable diff, and nothing for
# a review tool to read. The separator moved to \x1f, but a base blob still holding NULs makes the
# diff binary from ONE side, so the attribute is what actually restores review for the change that
# fixes it. An unreviewable source file is one whose next defect nobody can see.
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
